  "capacity": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - 33 cables, FS states none for the USCMH finger ducts. The channel clear cross-section, 22.3 mm high (the duct guide) by 59.76 mm deep (the well floor to the underside of the cover), divided by 39.9 mm2 a cable: the pooled ratio of the three FS ABS finger ducts whose capacity FS does state (CMH-SFD1U 48 in 1850 mm2, CMH-DFD1U 96 in 3700, CMH-SFD2U 124 in 5143). Those agree to within 8%, which is this figure's uncertainty at best; this is a different moulding. Across every FS manager the ratio runs 38.5 to 82.8 (the HD and UHD lines scale per rack unit), so it is fitted on the ABS ducts only."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - THE BODY BETWEEN THE EARS. The specification table gives 44.0 x 482.2 x 97.0 mm (1.73 x 18.98 x 3.81 in); the front view dimensions 44.3 high, 482.22 wide and the ear holes 31.74 apart, and draws the ear folds 23.0 mm in from each end, so the duct between them is 436.3. The ears are the ends of the base plate and are not drawn. 44.3 is taken for the height, the drawing over the table's rounded 44.0. `depth` STATES THE VENDOR OVERALL 97.00 (the top view's Ref figure): the fingers and the cover stand 61.46 in front of the plane of the ears (2.42 in on the dimensioned render) and the ribbed base 35.54 behind it at its deepest."
  },
  "color": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - \"Color: Black\". Every image FS publishes of the part is a render; it is drawn in CMH-SFD1U's shades, the cover a little lighter than the duct."
